        "id": 1129199
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-04-10T10:58:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I just discovered about jump tags, actually, so I\u0027m not sure ,-)\n\nRW does use shared memory, but I guess by the time it does, the jump tags would have been read out and are not useful anymore? Conversely, RO sets up the jump tags just before jumping to RW, so it would not be using shared memory at that time...\n\nThe problem though, is that shared_mem_size uses:\nsystem_usable_ram_end() - (uintptr_t)__shared_mem_buf\n\nand system_usable_ram_end() is\n(uintptr_t)jdata - jdata-\u003ejump_tag_total;\n\nSo, technically, we are underestimating a bit the required shared memory size... (shared_mem_acquire may fail even though SHARED_MEM_ACQUIRE_CHECK won\u0027t fail at compile time...)\n\nI guess we could fix this by actually allocating RAM for the jump tags?!",
      "parentUuid": "ae11c0b5_ee0eca00",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 21,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 23,
        "endChar": 40
      },
      "revId": "57c946ea3f933c01d965432bd2b2a657422c403b",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
